# Electron Forge Deployment Standards

## Objective
Establish consistent, secure, and efficient packaging and distribution processes for the Downlodr application across all supported platforms.

## Context
- Electron Forge 7.6+ for packaging and distribution
- Cross-platform builds (Windows, macOS, Linux)
- Code signing and notarization requirements
- Auto-update capabilities
- CI/CD integration for automated builds

## Rules

### Build Configuration

#### Forge Configuration Structure
- **Platform-specific makers**: Configure makers for each target platform
- **Security configuration**: Include proper security settings
- **Asset management**: Ensure all required assets are included
  ```typescript
  ✅ // forge.config.ts - Comprehensive configuration
  import { MakerPKG } from '@electron-forge/maker-pkg';
  import { MakerZIP } from '@electron-forge/maker-zip';
  import { MakerNSIS } from '@felixrieseberg/electron-forge-maker-nsis';
  import { VitePlugin } from '@electron-forge/plugin-vite';
  import { FusesPlugin } from '@electron-forge/plugin-fuses';
  import { FuseV1Options, FuseVersion } from '@electron/fuses';
  
  const config: ForgeConfig = {
    packagerConfig: {
      asar: true,
      icon: './src/Assets/AppLogo/256x256',
      name: 'Downlodr',
      executableName: 'Downlodr',
      extraResource: [
        './src/Assets/AppLogo',
        './yt-dlp.exe' // Platform-specific binaries
      ],
      ignore: [
        /^\/\.vscode/,
        /^\/\.git/,
        /^\/node_modules\/\.cache/,
        /^\/coverage/,
        /^\/\.nyc_output/
      ]
    },
    makers: [
      // macOS PKG installer
      new MakerPKG({
        identity: process.env.APPLE_IDENTITY,
        signing: {
          identity: process.env.APPLE_IDENTITY,
          entitlements: './entitlements.plist',
          'entitlements-inherit': './entitlements.plist',
          'gatekeeper-assess': false,
        },
      }),
      
      // Windows NSIS installer
      new MakerNSIS({
        async getAppBuilderConfig() {
          return {
            nsis: {
              oneClick: false,
              allowElevation: true,
              installerIcon: './src/Assets/AppLogo/256x256.ico',
              uninstallerIcon: './src/Assets/AppLogo/256x256.ico',
              allowToChangeInstallationDirectory: true,
              createDesktopShortcut: true,
              createStartMenuShortcut: true,
              deleteAppDataOnUninstall: false,
              perMachine: false,
              include: './installer.nsh'
            }
          };
        }
      }),
      
      // Cross-platform ZIP packages
      new MakerZIP({}, ['darwin', 'win32', 'linux'])
    ]
  };
  
  ❌ // Minimal configuration
  const config = {
    makers: [new MakerZIP()]
  };
  ```

#### Package.json Scripts
- **Consistent scripts**: Use standard script names across environments
- **Environment-specific builds**: Configure different build types
- **Version management**: Include proper versioning scripts
  ```json
  ✅ {
    "scripts": {
      "start": "electron-forge start",
      "package": "electron-forge package",
      "make": "electron-forge make",
      "make:all": "electron-forge make --platform=win32,darwin,linux",
      "make:win": "electron-forge make --platform=win32",
      "make:mac": "electron-forge make --platform=darwin",
      "make:linux": "electron-forge make --platform=linux",
      "publish": "electron-forge publish",
      "lint": "eslint --ext .ts,.tsx .",
      "build:prod": "NODE_ENV=production electron-forge make",
      "prepackage": "yarn lint && yarn test",
      "version:patch": "yarn version --patch && git push --tags",
      "version:minor": "yarn version --minor && git push --tags"
    }
  }
  
  ❌ // Incomplete scripts
  {
    "scripts": {
      "start": "electron ."
    }
  }
  ```

### Platform-Specific Configuration

#### Windows Configuration
- **NSIS installer**: Use NSIS for Windows installers
- **Code signing**: Configure Authenticode signing
- **Auto-updater**: Configure Squirrel.Windows updates
  ```typescript
  ✅ // Windows-specific configuration
  new MakerNSIS({
    async getAppBuilderConfig() {
      return {
        nsis: {
          artifactName: '${productName}-${version}-${arch}.${ext}',
          oneClick: false,
          allowElevation: true,
          installerIcon: './src/Assets/AppLogo/256x256.ico',
          uninstallerIcon: './src/Assets/AppLogo/256x256.ico',
          allowToChangeInstallationDirectory: true,
          createDesktopShortcut: true,
          createStartMenuShortcut: true,
          shortcutName: 'Downlodr',
          uninstallDisplayName: 'Downlodr',
          deleteAppDataOnUninstall: false,
          warningsAsErrors: false,
          perMachine: false,
          include: './installer.nsh',
          // Code signing configuration
          sign: process.env.WINDOWS_SIGN_TOOL,
          signDlls: true
        }
      };
    }
  })
  
  ❌ // Minimal Windows configuration
  new MakerNSIS({})
  ```

#### macOS Configuration
- **PKG installer**: Use PKG for macOS distribution
- **Code signing**: Configure Apple Developer ID signing
- **Notarization**: Include notarization process
  ```typescript
  ✅ // macOS-specific configuration
  new MakerPKG({
    identity: process.env.APPLE_IDENTITY,
    signing: {
      identity: process.env.APPLE_IDENTITY,
      entitlements: './entitlements.plist',
      'entitlements-inherit': './entitlements.plist',
      'gatekeeper-assess': false,
      'signature-flags': 'library'
    },
    // Notarization configuration
    notarize: {
      tool: 'notarytool',
      appleId: process.env.APPLE_ID,
      appleIdPassword: process.env.APPLE_PASSWORD,
      teamId: process.env.APPLE_TEAM_ID
    }
  })
  
  // entitlements.plist
  ✅ <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
  <!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
  <plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
      <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
      <false/>
      <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
      <false/>
      <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
      <false/>
      <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
      <false/>
    </dict>
  </plist>
  
  ❌ // No signing configuration
  new MakerPKG({})
  ```

### Security Configuration

#### Electron Fuses
- **Security fuses**: Configure Electron fuses for enhanced security
- **Feature restrictions**: Disable unnecessary Electron features
- **Runtime security**: Enhance runtime security
  ```typescript
  ✅ new FusesPlugin({
    version: FuseVersion.V1,
    [FuseV1Options.RunAsNode]: false,
    [FuseV1Options.EnableCookieEncryption]: true,
    [FuseV1Options.EnableNodeOptionsEnvironmentVariable]: false,
    [FuseV1Options.EnableNodeCliInspectArguments]: false,
    [FuseV1Options.EnableEmbeddedAsarIntegrityValidation]: true,
    [FuseV1Options.OnlyLoadAppFromAsar]: true,
    [FuseV1Options.LoadBrowserProcessSpecificV8Snapshot]: false
  })
  
  ❌ // Default/insecure fuse configuration
  new FusesPlugin({
    version: FuseVersion.V1,
    [FuseV1Options.RunAsNode]: true // Security risk
  })
  ```

#### Asset Protection
- **ASAR integrity**: Enable ASAR integrity validation
- **Resource protection**: Protect application resources
- **Binary inclusion**: Securely include external binaries
  ```typescript
  ✅ // Secure asset configuration
  packagerConfig: {
    asar: {
      unpack: '*.{node,dll,dylib,so}' // Unpack native modules
    },
    extraResource: [
      {
        from: './binaries',
        to: 'binaries',
        filter: ['**/*'] // Include all binary files
      }
    ],
    // Exclude development files
    ignore: [
      /^\/\.vscode/,
      /^\/\.git/,
      /^\/src\/.*\.test\./,
      /^\/coverage/,
      /^\/\.nyc_output/,
      /^\/docs/
    ]
  }
  
  ❌ // Insecure asset handling
  packagerConfig: {
    asar: false, // No protection
    extraResource: ['./'] // Include everything
  }
  ```

### Build Optimization

#### Size Optimization
- **Bundle analysis**: Analyze and optimize bundle size
- **Dependency optimization**: Exclude unnecessary dependencies
- **Asset optimization**: Compress and optimize assets
  ```typescript
  ✅ // Size optimization configuration
  packagerConfig: {
    // Exclude development dependencies
    ignore: [
      /^\/node_modules\/.*\/test/,
      /^\/node_modules\/.*\/\.nyc_output/,
      /^\/node_modules\/.*\/coverage/,
      /^\/node_modules\/.*\/docs/,
      /^\/node_modules\/.*\/examples/,
      /^\/node_modules\/@types/,
      /^\/node_modules\/typescript/,
      /^\/node_modules\/eslint/
    ],
    
    // Prune dependencies
    prune: true,
    
    // Optimize for production
    derefSymlinks: true
  }
  
  // Vite configuration for renderer optimization
  export default defineConfig({
    build: {
      minify: 'terser',
      rollupOptions: {
        external: ['electron'],
        output: {
          manualChunks: {
            vendor: ['react', 'react-dom'],
            ui: ['@radix-ui/react-dialog', '@radix-ui/react-toast']
          }
        }
      }
    }
  });
  
  ❌ // No optimization
  packagerConfig: {
    prune: false,
    ignore: []
  }
  ```

#### Performance Configuration
- **Parallel builds**: Enable parallel processing when possible
- **Caching**: Use build caching for faster builds
- **Progressive builds**: Optimize for incremental builds
  ```typescript
  ✅ // Performance optimization
  const config: ForgeConfig = {
    // Enable parallel builds
    buildConcurrency: os.cpus().length,
    
    // Cache configuration
    plugins: [
      new VitePlugin({
        build: [
          {
            entry: 'src/main.ts',
            config: 'vite.main.config.ts',
            target: 'main'
          }
        ],
        renderer: [
          {
            name: 'main_window',
            config: 'vite.renderer.config.ts'
          }
        ]
      })
    ]
  };
  
  ❌ // No performance considerations
  const config = {
    plugins: [new VitePlugin({})]
  };
  ```

### CI/CD Integration

#### GitHub Actions Configuration
- **Multi-platform builds**: Build for all target platforms
- **Artifact management**: Properly handle build artifacts
- **Release automation**: Automate release process
  ```yaml
  ✅ # .github/workflows/build.yml
  name: Build and Release
  
  on:
    push:
      tags: ['v*']
    pull_request:
      branches: [main]
  
  jobs:
    build:
      strategy:
        matrix:
          os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest, macos-latest]
          
      runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
      
      steps:
        - uses: actions/checkout@v3
        
        - name: Setup Node.js
          uses: actions/setup-node@v3
          with:
            node-version: '20'
            cache: 'yarn'
            
        - name: Install dependencies
          run: yarn install --frozen-lockfile
          
        - name: Run tests
          run: yarn test
          
        - name: Run linting
          run: yarn lint
          
        - name: Build application
          run: yarn make
          env:
            APPLE_ID: ${{ secrets.APPLE_ID }}
            APPLE_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.APPLE_PASSWORD }}
            APPLE_TEAM_ID: ${{ secrets.APPLE_TEAM_ID }}
            
        - name: Upload artifacts
          uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3
          with:
            name: ${{ matrix.os }}-build
            path: out/make/**/*
  
  ❌ # Minimal CI configuration
  name: Build
  on: [push]
  jobs:
    build:
      runs-on: ubuntu-latest
      steps:
        - run: npm run build
  ```

#### Environment Configuration
- **Environment variables**: Proper environment variable management
- **Secret management**: Secure handling of signing certificates
- **Build variants**: Support different build configurations
  ```bash
  ✅ # Environment configuration
  # Production build
  NODE_ENV=production yarn make
  
  # Development build with debugging
  DEBUG=electron-forge:* yarn start
  
  # Release build with signing
  APPLE_ID=$APPLE_ID \
  APPLE_PASSWORD=$APPLE_PASSWORD \
  WINDOWS_SIGN_TOOL=$SIGN_TOOL \
  yarn make:all
  
  ❌ # No environment configuration
  yarn make # Uses default settings
  ```

### Post-Build Processing

#### Binary Verification
- **Signature verification**: Verify code signatures
- **Size checks**: Monitor build size changes
- **Dependency auditing**: Check for security vulnerabilities
  ```bash
  ✅ # Post-build verification scripts
  #!/bin/bash
  
  # Verify macOS signature
  codesign --verify --deep --strict out/make/pkg/darwin/x64/Downlodr-*.pkg
  
  # Verify Windows signature
  signtool verify /pa out/make/nsis/win32/x64/Downlodr-*.exe
  
  # Check bundle size
  ls -lh out/make/**/* | awk '{print $5, $9}' | sort -hr
  
  # Security audit
  yarn audit --audit-level moderate
  
  ❌ # No verification
  # Build completes without verification
  ```

## Exceptions
- **Development builds**: May skip signing and optimization
- **Testing environments**: May use simplified configurations
- **Emergency releases**: May bypass some checks with approval
- **Platform limitations**: Some features may not be available on all platforms

## Enforcement
- CI/CD pipeline enforcement
- Build size monitoring
- Security scanning in builds
- Code review for configuration changes

